{
  "category": "Flycatcher Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "It spits out POISONPOWDER to immobilize the enemy and then finishes it with a spray of ACID.",
      "version": "red"
    },
    {
      "text": "It spits out POISONPOWDER to immobilize the enemy and then finishes it with a spray of ACID.",
      "version": "blue"
    },
    {
      "text": "When hungry, it swallows anything that moves. Its hapless prey is melted inside by strong acids.",
      "version": "yellow"
    },
    {
      "text": "Even though it is filled with ACID, it does not melt because it also oozes a neutralizing fluid.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "If its prey is bigger than its mouth, it slices up the victim with sharp leaves, then eats every morsel.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "When it's hungry, it swings its razor-sharp leaves, slicing up any unlucky object nearby for food.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "WEEPINBELL has a large hook on its rear end. At night, the POKéMON hooks on to a tree branch and goes to sleep. If it moves around in its sleep, it may wake up to find itself on the ground.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "WEEPINBELL has a large hook on its rear end. At night, the POKéMON hooks on to a tree branch and goes to sleep. If it moves around in its sleep, it may wake up to find itself on the ground.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "At night, a WEEPINBELL hangs on to a tree branch with its hooked rear and sleeps. If it moves around in its sleep, it may wake up to find itself on the ground.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "The leafy parts act as cutters for slashing foes. It spits a fluid that dissolves everything.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
